he following is shared with all the firm's employees:\\n\\n### DEP Guidelines\\n\\n- Be step-by-step, minimal ambiguity.\\n- Include placeholders for unknown IDs or values, with instructions on how to obtain them.\\n- Note external dependencies and how to validate results.\\n- Account for rollbacks, cleanup, and testing.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"A new Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) has been submitted for review. Please analyze the following DEP and respond with only \\\"APPROVE\\\" if you approve it, or \\\"DENY\\\" followed by your reasoning if you deny it.\\n\\n---BEGIN USER CLARIFICATION HISTORY---\\nQuestion: Hello! I am your Chief of Staff, here to help manage and execute your software or project needs. What would you like me to create or assist you with today?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 1) For the restricted pages (meeting minutes, financials, etc.), should every neighborhood resident have their own login, or will a few board members share access on behalf of everyone? If multiple roles are needed (e.g., resident vs. board), please describe them.\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 2) How would you like to update news, events, and page content? Are you looking for a very simple in-browser editor such as WordPress or Squarespace, or are you comfortable with a custom admin dashboard we build from scratch?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 3) Do you already have a domain name or hosting service in mind, or would you like recommendations and technical setup from scratch?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\nQuestion: 4) Do you have any existing logo, color scheme, or design inspiration you would like us to incorporate into the site?\\nResponse: undefined\\n\\n---END USER CLARIFICATION HISTORY---\\n\\n---BEGIN DEP---\\nDeterministically Executable Plan (DEP) – HOA Website MVP\\n========================================================\\n\\n0. Scope & Goal  \\n   Build and deploy a secure, low-cost HOA website (dunbaroakshoa.com) that lets non-technical Board members update content while protecting resident-only information.\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n1. Recommended Technology Stack\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFrontend         : Next.js 13 (App Router, React 18, TypeScript) – free tier on Vercel  \\nStyling/UI       : Tailwind CSS (utility, zero cost)  \\nAuth / DB / CMS  : Supabase (PostgreSQL, Storage, Auth) – generous free tier  \\nAdmin UI         : Built-in Supabase Table Editor + a lightweight in-site “Admin Portal” page  \\nDeployment       : Vercel (Git-based CI/CD, automatic HTTPS) – free tier  \\nCLI Tools        : supabase CLI, vercel CLI, pnpm (or npm/yarn)  \\nOptional E-mail  : Supabase free e-mail auth (magic-link); custom SMTP can be plugged-in later.\\n\\nWhy: All services have forever-free tiers that comfortably fit HOA traffic; simple RBAC; no servers to maintain; Board can edit data in a spreadsheet-like Supabase UI.\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n2. Roles & Access Model\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRole      | AuthN | Privileges\\n----------|-------|-----------------------------------------------\\nGuest     | none  | View public pages (Home, Contact, Bylaws, Schools)\\nResident  | login | View protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\nAdmin     | login | All resident rights + create/update/delete content/files, manage users\\n\\nAuthN Flow:  \\n• E-mail + magic-link (Supabase).  \\n• Board invites a user (Supabase dashboard or Admin Portal) → user receives link → sets password (optional).  \\n• Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) enforces:  \\n  – role = 'admin' for board members (custom claim in JWT).  \\n  – Residents default to role = 'resident'.\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n3. Content & Page Structure\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n/                Home (public, dynamic hero + latest News)  \\n/contact          Contact-Us form (public, sends e-mail via Formspree or Vercel Edge Function)  \\n/bylaws           Static Markdown + optional PDF (public)  \\n/schools          Static Markdown (public)  \\n/dues             Markdown/HTML + file attachments (protected)  \\n/annual-meetings  List of meeting minutes stored as PDFs in Supabase Storage (protected)  \\n/news-events      List + detail pages (Markdown or rich-text via Supabase) (protected)  \\n\\nNav bar shows menu items based on role.\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n4. Content Update Strategy (No-Code)\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\nA. Supabase Table “pages”  \\n   columns: id, slug, title, content_markdown, isProtected, updated_at.  \\n   Board edits via Supabase Table Editor (spreadsheet UI) = immediate site update (SWR fetch).\\n\\nB. Supabase Table “news_events”  \\n   columns: id, title, body_markdown, event_date, attachment_url, updated_at.\\n\\nC. Supabase Storage “documents/” bucket  \\n   RLS policy: resident or admin can SELECT; only admin can INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.  \\n   Board uploads new PDFs directly in Supabase Storage UI or via Admin Portal drag-and-drop.\\n\\nD. Optional Git-based fallback – markdown files in /content folder for rarely-changed public pages (Bylaws, Schools).\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n5. Hosting & Deployment Steps\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n(All commands deterministic; replace ${VARIABLE} where noted.)\\n\\n1. Local Setup  \\n```bash\\npnpm create next-app@latest dunbaroakshoa --ts --app --tailwind\\ncd dunbaroakshoa\\npnpm add @supabase/supabase-js @supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs\\npnpm add -D supabase vercel\\n```\\n\\n2. Initialize Git  \\n```bash\\ngit init\\ngit remote add origin git@github.com:dunbar-oaks/hoa-site.git\\n```\\n\\n3. Supabase Project  \\n   a. Dashboard → “New project” (Organization=Personal/free).  \\n   b. Set DB password ${DB_PASSWORD}.  \\n   c. Note Project URL & anon/public API Key.  \\n   d. Create tables “pages”, “news_events”.  \\n   e. Create storage bucket “documents”.  \\n   f. SQL:  \\n```sql\\nalter table auth.users add column role text default 'resident';\\ncreate policy \\\"Residents view public+protected pages\\\"\\n  on pages for select using (\\n    isProtected = false OR jwt_claims()->>'role' IN ('resident','admin')\\n  );\\n-- Similar policies for news_events and storage bucket.\\n```\\n\\n4. Environment Vars (.env.local)  \\n``` \\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<PROJECT>.supabase.co\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<SUPABASE_ANON_KEY>\\n```\\n\\n5. Implement Auth & RBAC in Next.js  \\n   • Create supabaseClient.ts.  \\n   • Wrap root layout with SessionContextProvider.  \\n   • Use useUser() hook to guard pages; 302 redirect guests trying to access protected routes.\\n\\n6. Build Admin Portal (/admin)  \\n   • Only role='admin' can access.  \\n   • CRUD UI built with React-Table & react-hook-form connected to Supabase.\\n\\n7. Contact Form (Edge Function)  \\n```bash\\nvercel functions add contact-email\\n# within api/contact.ts send e-mail via Resend (free 100/day).\\n```\\n\\n8. Vercel Deployment  \\n```bash\\nvercel login\\nvercel link --project dunbaroakshoa\\nvercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL ...\\nvercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY ...\\nvercel --prod\\n```\\n\\n9. Custom Domain  \\n   • Vercel Dashboard → Settings → Domains → “dunbaroakshoa.com”.  \\n   • Update DNS at registrar to Vercel’s A & CNAME records (deterministic values shown by Vercel).  \\n   • HTTPS auto-provisioned.\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n6. Security Best Practices Implemented\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n• HTTPS enforced by Vercel.  \\n• Supabase RLS policies (principle of least privilege).  \\n• JWT in http-only cookies via @supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs—mitigates XSS token theft.  \\n• CSP headers and rate-limiting via Vercel middleware (@vercel/edge – 100 req/min per IP).  \\n• Secrets stored in Vercel Environments, NOT in repo.  \\n• Regular backups: Supabase nightly (free).  \\n• Form anti-spam via hCaptcha (free).\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n7. Recurring Cost Estimate (per month)\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n• Vercel Hobby Plan: $0 (includes 100 GB-hrs, 100 GB bandwidth)  \\n• Supabase Free Tier: $0 (500 MB DB, 1 GB storage, 50 GB bandwidth)  \\n• Domain Renewal: ≈ $12/yr → $1/mo  \\n• Resend e-mail (free → $0–3/mo if >3 k e-mails)  \\n\\nTotal expected monthly recurring cost: ≈ $1.\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\n8. OFAAT-Style Work Packages\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\nWP-01 Scaffold Project – create repo, Next.js base, Tailwind configured.\\nWP-02 Supabase Setup – project, tables, RLS, storage bucket, env vars.\\nWP-03 Auth Integration – supabase client, session provider, login/signup pages.\\nWP-04 Public Pages – Home, Contact, Bylaws, Schools (markdown rendering).\\nWP-05 Protected Route Guard – /dues, /annual-meetings, /news-events, auth gating.\\nWP-06 News & Events CRUD UI – resident view + admin portal edit forms.\\nWP-07 Documents Module – upload & download PDFs in Supabase Storage with RLS.\\nWP-08 Contact Edge Function – serverless e-mail sender + spam protection.\\nWP-09 Styling & Responsive Design – polish navigation, branding.\\nWP-10 CI/CD & Domain – Vercel project hookup, custom domain, HTTPS.\\nWP-11 Security Hardening – rate limiting, CSP headers, dependency audit.\\nWP-12 Smoke Tests – Cypress e2e tests for auth flow and content access.\\nWP-13 Docs & Handoff – README with update in